# Deliberate bidirectional-control fixtures. These two tests embed U+202E
# (RIGHT-TO-LEFT OVERRIDE) in a remote deck's host name on purpose, to prove
# the desktop label rendering strips it. Semgrep's
# generic.unicode.security.bidi.contains-bidirectional-characters rule cannot
# tell a fixture from a Trojan-source attack, so it reported 3 blocking
# findings on every run (issue #808). Ignoring the two files, not the rule,
# keeps the rule live for the rest of the tree. Both files are upstream's
# (vfarcic/dot-agent-deck, PR 1035), which runs no Semgrep, so an inline
# `nosemgrep` marker there would be a sync conflict for nothing.
desktop/src/components/EndpointsPanel.test.tsx
desktop/e2e/decks.spec.ts
